      "id": "df1472b39a60123c9996b58c01293345fdf20288",
      "message": "OTA-1854 fixup \u2014 the new suite stops spending ota1484's fixture ratchet\n\nCI run 2234 shard 4/4 was RED on ota1484APinStatesAClaim: \"bare\ncurrentLocationId fixtures may only shrink\", expected <= 54, received 55. The\n55th was mine \u2014 \u00a7D's `state()` helper fed `onStoreChange` a store shape with a\nbare `currentLocationId` and no `placedAt`.\n\nMY LOCAL VALIDATION MISSED IT, AND THE REASON MATTERS. I chose the suites to\nrun by the IMPORT GRAPH of the changed modules. ota1484's ratchet does not\nimport anything \u2014 it walks the whole __tests__ directory and reads bytes. Any\nNEW test file is in its scope no matter what it imports, so an import-graph\nselection can never see it. The fast surface is now run in full below.\n\nTHE FIX SPENDS NO RATCHET. \u00a7D's job is \"did OTA-1853's voice survive OTA-1854's\ncut\", and the artwork and audio marks answer it through the SAME\nannotateMemory door while taking a plain string id \u2014 no store shape, no bare\nfixture, no permanent project-wide allowance spent. Rooms keep their coverage\nwhere it belongs, in ota1853TheRoomBoundarySpeaks \u00a7G, which owns that claim.\nD1 now also pins the code (memCodeForId of the asset key), which the previous\nversion did not.\n\nRe-baselining 54 -> 55 was the alternative and was rejected: the ratchet is a\nshrink-only anti-growth guard, and buying a slot to re-prove a claim another\nsuite already holds is a poor trade.\n\nNo production file changed in this commit.\n\nValidation on this tree: FULL FAST SURFACE 1349/1349 suites, 15,376 passed,\n3 skipped, 0 failed. 22/22 local gates, typecheck source + test ratchet, full\nlint. No Heavy CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-20T02:42:45Z",
